Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.12,0:00:02.73,Caption,,0,0,0,,Energy gets wasted for a boring reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.85,0:00:06.94,Caption,,0,0,0,,Someone has a forecast, but nobody trusts it enough to act.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.12,0:00:11.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,In September I built Agentic Arbiter, an agent for data-centre cooling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.32,0:00:14.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,It looks at 238 real data centres across America.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.42,0:00:19.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,Data centres run chillers even when the air outside is already cold enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.42,0:00:24.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,So it decides, hour by hour, when switching them off is actually safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.42,0:00:28.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,Here it made no unsafe calls, where the old controller made one.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.02,0:00:32.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,That is four hundred extra free-cooling hours a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.52,0:00:33.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,And it grades itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.10,0:00:37.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,Here it missed its own target, and it says so.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.92,0:00:43.19,Caption,,0,0,0,,Second of eight hundred and forty-two teams, out of nearly four thousand people.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.31,0:00:45.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,The UN-backed Cool Coalition featured it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.92,0:00:48.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,Next I want it running on real sites.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.02,0:00:51.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,Then I looked at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.14,0:00:56.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,Pakistan has solar on millions of roofs, but the grid cannot see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.52,0:00:57.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,I asked twenty-one families.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.11,0:01:03.24,Caption,,0,0,0,,Seven of the ten with solar have changed habits or are getting a battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.42,0:01:09.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,So I am building a Solar Home Agent, for homes that cannot sell their spare power.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.52,0:01:14.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,Go over two hundred units in a month, and every single unit costs more.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.92,0:01:19.71,Caption,,0,0,0,,Moving a few jobs into the sun keeps this home under that line.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.83,0:01:22.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,About five thousand rupees this month.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.22,0:01:25.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,It picks when to run the motor, and says why.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.02,0:01:30.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,Thirteen of them said they would only trust an app that explains itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.02,0:01:35.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,So when it is not sure, it says no, and tells you why.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.02,0:01:40.84,Caption,,0,0,0,,It still wastes most of its midday sun. Storage is what closes that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.02,0:01:44.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,This is a simulation, with every assumption written down.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.52,0:01:48.37,Caption,,0,0,0,,Next, five to ten homes in Islamabad over WhatsApp.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.49,0:01:52.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,Then one neighbourhood forecast, built with our distribution company.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.52,0:01:54.87,Caption,,0,0,0,,The solar is already on Pakistan's roofs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.99,0:01:58.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,I want the grid to see it, and trust it.
